WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.386 --> 00:00:16.010
and Amy spent every day together, both of them enjoying the companionship of an old friend and familiar

2
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:23.195
conversation. However, Amy sensed that Laurie was holding something back, and she had a good idea it had

3
00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:23.955
to do with Jo.

4
00:00:24.856 --> 00:00:31.168
One afternoon, while the two friends were relaxing—Amy sketching a paradise-like scene of fruit trees and birds while

5
00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:34.310
Laurie flipped through a book—she decided to ask Laurie about it.

6
00:00:35.771 --> 00:00:38.633
"Laurie?" Amy called in her most ladylike voice.

7
00:00:38.653 --> 00:00:41.674
"Did something happen between you and Jo?"

8
00:00:42.955 --> 00:00:45.577
Shutting his book, Laurie said, "What makes you ask?"

9
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:54.102
Carefully choosing her words, Amy replied, "You used to be best friends, but I've noticed that whenever I

10
00:00:54.182 --> 00:01:00.322
mention her name or talk about something to do with Jo, you either change the subject or avoid

11
00:01:00.342 --> 00:01:01.523
the topic altogether."

12
00:01:02.544 --> 00:01:06.007
Laurie looked out at the scenery Amy was sketching and said nothing at first.

13
00:01:06.487 --> 00:01:09.229
Then, he said quietly, "She broke my heart, Amy."

14
00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.773
Setting aside her sketchbook, Amy walked over and sat next to him.

15
00:01:13.793 --> 00:01:17.817
"Sometimes talking about it can help," she said kindly.

16
00:01:18.938 --> 00:01:23.582
So Laurie began to tell her everything that happened, and Amy listened sympathetically.

17
00:01:25.643 --> 00:01:29.666
Back home, Jo knew from Amy's letter that she had run into Laurie in Italy.

18
00:01:30.287 --> 00:01:33.929
But Jo did not have a clue the two of them were talking about her at that moment.

19
00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:40.714
Her thoughts were otherwise occupied as she worked frantically, her fingers numb and stiff, putting the finishing touches

20
00:01:40.774 --> 00:01:42.375
on the last paragraph of her story.

21
00:01:43.176 --> 00:01:48.079
Satisfied with the ending, Jo threw on her coat and headed toward the office of the Volcano magazine.

22
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.864
The Volcano printed trashy stories, but Jo knew that's what sold and she needed the money.

23
00:01:55.772 --> 00:02:00.213
Upon returning from the Volcano, Jo put her recent earnings into the box she had been saving her

24
00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:00.633
money in.

25
00:02:01.394 --> 00:02:02.254
It was almost full.

26
00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:04.654
She emptied the box and began counting.

27
00:02:04.674 --> 00:02:09.756
"Three hundred and fifty-two dollars and twenty cents," she calculated.

28
00:02:09.776 --> 00:02:11.716
"That should be enough for our trip."

29
00:02:12.757 --> 00:02:17.698
Suddenly feeling as though a large weight was lifted off her shoulders, Jo threw her coat back on.

30
00:02:18.678 --> 00:02:21.139
This time, she headed toward the coach office in town.

31
00:02:22.679 --> 00:02:28.005
After his intimate conversation with Amy, Laurie also felt as though a burden was lifted from his heart.

32
00:02:28.646 --> 00:02:33.228
He still thought of Jo, but not as often, and he noticed that he had begun to enjoy

33
00:02:33.288 --> 00:02:33.848
life again.

34
00:02:34.788 --> 00:02:39.330
Laurie had already been in Europe for over two months but only then did he feel as though

35
00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.731
his vacation was beginning.

36
00:02:41.751 --> 00:02:46.073
Amy was touched that Laurie had opened up and shared his heartbreaking experience with her.

37
00:02:46.813 --> 00:02:50.895
She knew, everyone did, that Laurie had had a crush on Jo for many years.

38
00:02:51.795 --> 00:02:56.209
She also knew that it was one-sided, and Jo never looked at Laurie as anything more than her

39
00:02:56.249 --> 00:02:57.750
best friend and a brother figure.

40
00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:00.231
"Miss Amy?

41
00:03:00.751 --> 00:03:03.892
Mr. Laurence is here," the servant announced through Amy's door.

42
00:03:03.912 --> 00:03:05.053
"Thank you.

43
00:03:05.413 --> 00:03:05.913
Tell Mr.

44
00:03:05.933 --> 00:03:11.396
Laurence I'll be right down," Amy called back, grinning at the thought of someone calling Laurie "Mr.

45
00:03:11.436 --> 00:03:17.238
Laurence." Tonight Laurie was taking Amy to the opera, so she had made an extra effort to look

46
00:03:17.278 --> 00:03:17.759
her best.

47
00:03:18.759 --> 00:03:24.013
Laurie seemed to notice how beautiful Amy looked, because upon seeing her walking down the stairs, he remarked,

48
00:03:24.513 --> 00:03:27.374
"I'm going to need a stick to keep all the young men away from you."

49
00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:32.075
Suddenly feeling shy, Amy blushed as she took his outstretched hand.

50
00:03:33.335 --> 00:03:39.397
Beth and Jo were not looking as lovely as Amy, but they were having a fantastic time as

51
00:03:39.437 --> 00:03:43.978
they poked their heads out of the coach to catch sight of endless rows of cornfields in Kansas.

52
00:03:44.778 --> 00:03:49.600
Their journey to California had begun three days ago, and it would take another week to arrive at

53
00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:50.480
their destination.

54
00:03:51.688 --> 00:03:57.170
The girls, however, were enjoying every moment as they saw new scenery, met interesting people, and heard a

55
00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.930
variety of accents along the way.

56
00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:05.652
"It's a shame neither of us can draw like Amy," Jo kept saying, because she wanted somehow to

57
00:04:05.692 --> 00:04:09.093
preserve the memorable sights to remind herself of this trip in the future.

58
00:04:10.593 --> 00:04:13.794
However, Beth's reply made it clear why she was taking this trip.

59
00:04:13.814 --> 00:04:19.596
"If we spent our time concentrating on one sight, we might miss out on the others.

60
00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.721
I'd rather see everything once than see the same scene over and over again.

61
00:04:25.502 --> 00:04:31.383
Besides, the picture we take with our heart is always so much more precious than the ones we

62
00:04:31.423 --> 00:04:33.564
capture with a brush, don't you think?"

63
00:04:35.344 --> 00:04:40.566
Closing their eyes as the wind blew against their faces, Jo and Beth breathed the Midwestern air in

64
00:04:40.626 --> 00:04:45.587
deeply. Back home, Meg and Mother sat having tea and knitting clothes for the baby.

65
00:04:46.348 --> 00:04:50.425
Meg's stomach was big, bigger than Mother's had been during each of her pregnancies.

66
00:04:51.745 --> 00:04:54.866
"Meg, I don't mean to alarm you, but has Dr.

67
00:04:54.906 --> 00:04:57.047
Bangs mentioned anything about your baby?"

68
00:04:57.387 --> 00:04:57.887
Mother said.

69
00:04:57.907 --> 00:05:00.828
"Why? Do you think there is something wrong?"

70
00:05:01.048 --> 00:05:01.928
Meg asked worriedly.

71
00:05:03.048 --> 00:05:08.870
"Dr. Bangs is much more knowledgeable in these matters, but I wouldn't be surprised if you were carrying

72
00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.431
more than one," Mother said with a smile.

73
00:05:12.731 --> 00:05:14.812
Meg dropped her knitting and stared openmouthed.

74
00:05:14.832 --> 00:05:16.032
"You mean twins?

75
00:05:16.712 --> 00:05:18.093
I might be carrying twins?"

76
00:05:18.954 --> 00:05:25.400
Shrugging her shoulders, Mother replied, "It's not so unusual, Meg, and you seem quite large to be having

77
00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.561
just one baby."

78
00:05:27.481 --> 00:05:32.646
Rubbing her big belly, Meg repeated disbelievingly, "There might be two babies inside?"

79
00:05:33.887 --> 00:05:39.451
Not realizing that she might become an aunt to two babies at once, Amy, after enjoying several evenings

80
00:05:39.512 --> 00:05:44.556
of dancing and partying, was becoming increasingly irritated at Laurie's playboy approach to life.

81
00:05:45.288 --> 00:05:49.251
They sat in the sitting room of the villa Aunt March had rented having a serious chat.

82
00:05:49.891 --> 00:05:51.292
"When are you returning home?"

83
00:05:51.592 --> 00:05:52.033
she asked.

84
00:05:53.274 --> 00:05:55.655
"I haven't really thought about it," he answered, shrugging.

85
00:05:56.436 --> 00:05:57.637
"What about graduation?

86
00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.538
What about finding a job?"

87
00:05:59.838 --> 00:06:00.458
she continued.

88
00:06:00.478 --> 00:06:02.360
"I don't have to work, really.

89
00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:06.903
Grandfather can provide me with all that I need," Laurie replied as if he didn't care.

90
00:06:08.164 --> 00:06:12.827
Amy, who was also knitting (all the March girls enjoyed it as a hobby), began clicking her needles

91
00:06:12.867 --> 00:06:14.268
faster and kept her mouth shut.

92
00:06:15.016 --> 00:06:16.638
"Are you upset about something?"

93
00:06:16.898 --> 00:06:18.880
Laurie asked, noticing Amy's coldness.

94
00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:21.402
"Yes," she replied curtly.

95
00:06:21.422 --> 00:06:24.785
"You are the laziest boy I've ever met."

96
00:06:25.886 --> 00:06:28.348
Startled, Laurie asked her why she thought that.

97
00:06:29.629 --> 00:06:34.933
Putting her knitting down, Amy said, "Just because you're rich doesn't mean you should waste your life away.

98
00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:39.217
There is so much more for someone clever like you to do in this world.

99
00:06:39.878 --> 00:06:42.916
Money isn't everything, Theodore Laurence!"

100
00:06:42.936 --> 00:06:47.598
With those words, Laurie, but more so Amy, was shocked to discover how much she had changed in

101
00:06:47.618 --> 00:06:48.238
the last year.

102
00:06:48.258 --> 00:06:54.701
"Why, Amy March, I never thought I'd hear you say that," Laurie said nastily.

103
00:06:54.721 --> 00:07:00.924
"Well, that's how I feel, and shame on you for exploiting and wasting your grandfather's money this way,"

104
00:07:01.244 --> 00:07:02.084
Amy snapped at him.

105
00:07:03.245 --> 00:07:06.966
Standing up, Laurie said, "I can and will do as I choose."

106
00:07:06.986 --> 00:07:10.528
"Then do it," Amy said in a shaky voice.

107
00:07:11.388 --> 00:07:14.413
"But don't do it around me, because I won't stand for it."

108
00:07:15.094 --> 00:07:19.179
Grabbing his coat and hat, Laurie said coolly, "Take care, Amy.

109
00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.544
It was lovely to spend time with you, but I'm afraid the fun is over."

110
00:07:23.385 --> 00:07:24.507
And he walked out the door.
